.TH CHIKO 1 "2026-09-26" "chiko 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chiko \- beautiful terminal UI client for gRPC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chiko
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ host : port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chiko
is a terminal user interface for exploring and calling gRPC services.  It
uses server reflection to discover the services and methods a server
exposes, lets the request payload and metadata be edited interactively, and
displays the response in a scrollable output panel.
.PP
Sessions can be saved as bookmarks, grouped into categories, and recalled
later; every invocation is also kept in a history panel.
.PP
If a
.IR host : port
argument is given, chiko connects to that address on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-plaintext
Use plain-text HTTP/2 when connecting to the server, without TLS.  Enabled
by default.
.TP
.B \-insecure
Skip verification of the server certificate and host name.  Only meaningful
when TLS is used.
.TP
.BI \-cacert " file"
File containing the trusted root certificates used to verify the server.
.TP
.BI \-cert " file"
File containing the client certificate (public key) for mutual TLS.  Must be
given together with
.BR \-key .
.TP
.BI \-key " file"
File containing the client private key for mutual TLS.  Must be given
together with
.BR \-cert .
.TP
.BI \-d " data"
Contents of the request, as JSON.
.TP
.B \-allow\-unknown\-fields
Accept unknown fields in the JSON request instead of reporting an error.
.TP
.BI \-connect\-timeout " seconds"
Maximum time to wait for the connection to be established.  Defaults to 10.
.TP
.BI \-keepalive\-time " seconds"
Maximum idle time before a keepalive probe is sent.  Defaults to 0, meaning
no probes.
.TP
.BI \-max\-time " seconds"
Maximum total time for the whole operation.  Defaults to 0, meaning no
limit.
.TP
.BI \-max\-msg\-sz " bytes"
Maximum encoded size of a response message.  Defaults to 4194304.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/chiko
Configuration directory holding saved bookmarks and history.  When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset,
.I ~/.config/chiko
is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B chiko
exits with status 0 on success and 1 if the command line is invalid or the
interface cannot be started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grpcurl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at <https://github.com/felangga/chiko/issues>.
.SH AUTHOR
